{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfwhce2vgkQ2rwme5yiao","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard to look at the charts or waited for the rule to run.\n\n**Data:** The sample logs hold web requests with `timestamp`, `response` (the HTTP status, stored as text), `bytes`, `extension`, `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `clientip`, `host`, `machine.os`, `url` and `agent`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-494aab50 Web logs overview\" has five panels and defaults to the last 7 days. It's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-494aab50-web-logs-overview-0d5c954bf898.\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Responses by status code\n- Bytes by file extension\n- Top source countries\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-494aab50 5xx spike\" (id `e1fd4b3b-4547-4d88-ba6d-7eee86a8a6f4`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- It runs every minute and counts documents with `response.keyword` matching `5*` in the last 5 minutes.\n- It fires when that count is above 10.\n- It was created disabled and I then enabled it.\n- It has no actions attached, so a firing will only show up in Kibana's alert list, not as a notification."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":171,"cache_read_input_tokens":20370,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":171},"output_tokens":458,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"376f092e-331d-4d5b-9c05-6fc62ff44088","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:20:08.241Z","request_id":"req_011Cfwhcdq2FVcekDz6rhv3F"}
